\label{m0015_Cyclotron_motion}
Electrons moving in a circle in a magnetic field (\emph{cyclotron motion}). 
The electrons are produced by an electron gun at bottom, consisting of a hot cathode, a metal plate heated by a filament so it emits electrons, and a metal anode at a high voltage with a hole which accelerates the electrons into a beam. The electrons are normally invisible, but enough air has been left in the tube so that the air molecules glow pink when struck by the fast-moving electrons.
}
